<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Requiring two-factor authentication">
        <ol>
            <li>On <a href="/manage/users">Users</a>, select <strong>Two-Factor Settings</strong>.</li>
            <li>Turn on <strong>Require two-factor authentication for everyone</strong> at your company and confirm.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            The dialog lists <strong>Staff with two-factor authentication</strong> and who hasn't set it up yet.
            While it's required, people who haven't set it up are asked to before they can carry on, and nobody
            can turn it off on their own account.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Helping someone who can't sign in">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Forgotten password:</strong> on their profile's Account tab, select <strong>Send Password Reset Email</strong>,
                or set one on the Password tab.</li>
            <li><strong>Locked:</strong> select <strong>Unlock Account</strong>, or wait 15 minutes.</li>
            <li><strong>Never set a password:</strong> select <strong>Resend Invite</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Can't remember their username:</strong> they can sign in with their email address instead.</li>
            <li><strong>Wrong location:</strong> check they belong to the location they're choosing at sign-in.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
